Error [E2305]: This view points into `values`, which this function owns
  --> stored_lambda_returning_view_is_rejected_before_codegen.jet:8:23
    |
  8 |     callback :: () -> first(values)
    |                       ^^^^^
 Why: `values` is made here and freed when the function returns, so a read window into it would outlive what owns it — there'd be nothing left to look at
 Fix: Return an owned copy with `place.copy()` (for example `value[a..b].copy()`), or accept the source as a parameter so the caller keeps owning it
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2305
